@startuml llm_pipeline
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName Arial

title Полный pipeline LLM + Vector DB + формальные модели

rectangle "1. Sensor / State Layer\nrobot-agent status messages,\ntasks, batteries, routes" as state
database "2. Local Vector DB\nwarehouse_rules.json\nhashed embeddings + cosine search" as vectordb
rectangle "3. Strategic LLM Layer\nOllama on localhost\nweights, safety margin,\nblocked edges" as llm
rectangle "4. Tactical Game Layer\nContract Net auction\nCongestion game\nBest-response Nash profile" as game
rectangle "5. Distributed Operational Layer\nper-robot controllers\nA* planner, traffic rules,\ncollision checks" as control
rectangle "Webots Scene\nrobot/cargo translation,\nrotation and event logs" as webots

state --> vectordb : compact query
vectordb --> llm : retrieved rules
state --> llm : compact JSON state
llm --> game : Strategy
game --> control : assignment messages + routes
control --> webots : each robot moves itself
webots --> state : next tick status messages

note bottom of llm
The LLM does not directly drive motors.
It tunes strategic parameters for
formal decision models.
end note
@enduml
